---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="The purpose and governance of the Kwechiri programming language."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Project"
    title="A language with its own identity."
    lead="Kwechiri is an Igbo-first programming language and educational ecosystem under active development."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Kwechiri aims to make programming more accessible to Igbo speakers while
        maintaining a professional compiler architecture and a path to modern
        software ecosystems.
      </p>
      <p>
        Its long-term identity includes its own specification, compiler stages,
        runtime abstractions, Standard Library, tools, documentation, and
        educational model. The initial TypeScript compiler and JavaScript
        target are implementation choices, not the language definition.
      </p>

      <h2>Governance</h2>
      <p>
        The human project owner is the final authority for language identity,
        Igbo terminology, syntax, semantics, public APIs, branding, licensing,
        compatibility, publication, and releases.
      </p>
      <p>
        Engineering proceeds through explicit milestones. Material language
        changes require a documented decision, implementation, tests, review,
        and owner approval before closure.
      </p>

      <h2>Development status</h2>
      <p>
        Kwechiri runs through the Node.js CLI and a single-file browser
        playground, and has no public package release. VS Code integration,
        final terminology, and 1.0 compatibility remain future work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
